// =============================================================================
// chora.delivery.v1 — Assessment + Submission lifecycle events
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/architecture/adrs/adr-155-assessment-grading-dispatch.md
//   §"R+ Delivery State Machine" + §"In Scope for Phyllis demo"
// + .claude/rules/ddd-enforcement.md
// + chora-contracts/openapi/delivery-assessments.yaml
//
// Owning domain  : Content Delivery (chora_delivery database)
// Owning team    : Team 2 (Delivery)
// Topic prefix   : chora.delivery.assessment.* + chora.delivery.submission.*
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Two aggregates, two FSMs
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 1. Assessment — instructor-instantiated live run of a TestSet for a class/
//    cohort. Lifecycle:
//      DRAFT      → SCHEDULED (via /publish; requires scheduled_open_at >= now)
//      SCHEDULED  → OPEN      (auto-flip at scheduled_open_at; or admin override)
//      OPEN       → CLOSED    (auto-flip at scheduled_close_at OR all
//                              attempts exhausted)
//      CLOSED     → GRADING   (auto-trigger grading job after all submissions
//                              finalise OR timeout)
//      GRADING    → GRADED    (when grading_finalized.v1 received for all
//                              submissions)
//      GRADED     → RELEASED  (manual via /release-results; or auto if
//                              grading_config.auto_release=true)
//      any        → ARCHIVED  (manual; preserves immutable audit trail)
//
// 2. Submission — per-learner attempt against an Assessment. Lifecycle:
//      IN_PROGRESS → SUBMITTED (via /submit; or auto on time-out)
//      SUBMITTED   → GRADING   (assessment-level batch grading dispatches)
//      GRADING     → GRADED    (grading_finalized.v1 received)
//      GRADED      → RELEASED  (parent assessment released)
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Eight topics defined here
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// chora.delivery.assessment.created.v1     — POST /assessments lands
// chora.delivery.assessment.published.v1   — DRAFT → SCHEDULED
// chora.delivery.assessment.closed.v1      — OPEN → CLOSED (auto or admin)
// chora.delivery.assessment.released.v1    — GRADED → RELEASED
// chora.delivery.submission.started.v1     — learner starts an attempt
// chora.delivery.submission.submitted.v1   — learner finalises (triggers grading)
// chora.delivery.submission.graded.v1      — grading_finalized.v1 propagated to
//                                            the submission's state
// chora.delivery.submission.released.v1    — parent assessment release
//                                            propagated to this submission
//
// Composes with `chora.delivery.grading.*` topics in grading.proto. The
// boundary: assessment.* + submission.* describe lifecycle transitions;
// grading.* describes the grading-job sub-machine triggered by
// submission.submitted.v1 and consumed by submission.graded.v1.
//
// EVERY event embeds chora.common.v1.EventEnvelope as field 1.
// =============================================================================

